{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01124",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.57,
      "end_seconds": 4.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "Doctor, we're ready in room two, I've already taken the observations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.79,
      "end_seconds": 9.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "Perfect, thanks. Hello there, so what's the trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.14,
      "end_seconds": 17.52,
      "duration_seconds": 7.38,
      "text": "yeah, it's cramps in my calves at night i don't know what's causing it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 18.87,
      "end_seconds": 32.05,
      "duration_seconds": 13.18,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Oxygen saturation is 98 percent, weight 75 kilos. Respiratory rate 18, blood pressure 125 over 81, height 150 centimetres, pulse is 78 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.25,
      "end_seconds": 35.95,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.56,
      "end_seconds": 55.79,
      "duration_seconds": 1.23,
      "text": "since when exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.4,
      "end_seconds": 65.33,
      "duration_seconds": 7.93,
      "text": "about... well, about a year my family kept telling me to get it checked"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.09,
      "end_seconds": 70.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "Alright, is there something that settles it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.48,
      "end_seconds": 87.83,
      "duration_seconds": 16.35,
      "text": "Only walking about and stretching, and it's not much. I've had tingling in my feet too, for six months. About tingling in my feet, it comes and goes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.7,
      "end_seconds": 97.81,
      "duration_seconds": 8.11,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any redness of the leg, chest pain or shortness of breath?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.56,
      "end_seconds": 102.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "No, none that I've noticed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 103.06,
      "end_seconds": 107.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Right, right. Have you had back pain, by any chance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.91,
      "end_seconds": 111.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "no, um, no back pain"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.02,
      "end_seconds": 115.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.31,
      "end_seconds": 120.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "no, uh, that side's been fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.74,
      "end_seconds": 128.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.96,
      "end_seconds": 138.6,
      "duration_seconds": 7.64,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, I don't think I have any, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.63,
      "end_seconds": 152.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "Are there any illnesses in your family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.2,
      "end_seconds": 159.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.83,
      "text": "Okay, uh, so my grandfather had a stroke."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.75,
      "end_seconds": 164.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.35,
      "end_seconds": 183.58,
      "duration_seconds": 18.23,
      "text": "I've had diabetes for about ten years now. I took the morning off to come in today. Erm, you know, I've had high blood pressure for about ten years now. I've been putting this off for weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.5,
      "end_seconds": 190.97,
      "duration_seconds": 6.47,
      "text": "Alright, high blood pressure, that matches what I have here. Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.04,
      "end_seconds": 203.02,
      "duration_seconds": 9.98,
      "text": "I walk the dog every morning. I'm vegetarian and have been for years. I work in accounts at a hospital."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.69,
      "end_seconds": 206.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Did you ever have any procedures done?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 208.79,
      "end_seconds": 213.4,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "Just keyhole surgery on my gallbladder, two years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.88,
      "end_seconds": 228.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 232.73,
      "end_seconds": 242.7,
      "duration_seconds": 9.97,
      "text": "Yeah, it's glibenclamide, 5 milligrams, before breakfast for my sugar. I take valsartan, 80 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.22,
      "end_seconds": 244.06,
      "duration_seconds": 0.84,
      "text": "I follow."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 245.0,
      "end_seconds": 248.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "I take magnesium tablets, at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.93,
      "end_seconds": 252.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Alright, shall I start the examination?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 253.24,
      "end_seconds": 255.05,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "Yes, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.38,
      "end_seconds": 259.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Take a deep breath for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.29,
      "end_seconds": 282.4,
      "duration_seconds": 6.11,
      "text": "Both calves are soft and not tender, and the pulses at your feet are good."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.66,
      "end_seconds": 306.69,
      "duration_seconds": 22.03,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed. So, based on the history and the examination, it's hard to say. Night-time muscle cramps without a worrying cause is one possibility and a side effect of a medicine another, and I'd rather not commit yet. I'd like to arrange blood tests for muscle cramps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 307.56,
      "end_seconds": 311.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "Um, how long will it it take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.43,
      "end_seconds": 319.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.51,
      "text": "Come back in four weeks. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 320.68,
      "end_seconds": 323.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thanks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.69,
      "end_seconds": 328.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.19,
      "text": "Take care now."
    }
  ]
}